# Scoped EOL pinning for the blocker-closure package.
#
# SHA256SUMS.txt in this folder records SHA256 over the exact bytes of the 13
# markdown deliverables. The repository-wide setting core.autocrlf=true would
# otherwise check these files out as CRLF on Windows, so a reviewer's
# `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` would report 13 mismatches that are pure
# line-ending artifacts, not content drift.
#
# `text eol=lf` keeps the blob in the index as LF (unchanged) and forces the
# working-tree copy to LF on every platform, so the recorded hashes verify
# byte-for-byte on Linux, macOS and Windows alike.
#
# Scope is deliberately limited to this folder and the sibling 08- folder so
# that no pre-existing file in the repository has its checkout behaviour
# changed by this commit.
docs/phases/anatomy-driven-geometry-poc/08-dec05-visual-direction-review/*.md text eol=lf
docs/phases/anatomy-driven-geometry-poc/08-dec05-visual-direction-review/*.txt text eol=lf
docs/phases/anatomy-driven-geometry-poc/09-blocker-closure-auth08/*.md text eol=lf
docs/phases/anatomy-driven-geometry-poc/09-blocker-closure-auth08/*.txt text eol=lf
docs/phases/anatomy-driven-geometry-poc/10-decision-records/*.md text eol=lf

# P1-VR-ARCH-1 host-only tools and evidence (2026-11-26).
#
# docs/research/human-template-reuse/evidence/host-proof/SHA256SUMS.txt and its
# tooling-manifest.md record SHA-256 over exact bytes (logs, reports and PNGs).
# `-text` switches end-of-line conversion off in both directions for these two
# new folders only, so the recorded hashes verify on every platform and no
# pre-existing file changes its checkout behaviour. The folder mixes text and
# PNG, which is why it uses `-text` rather than the `text eol=lf` used above.
tools/human-template-poc/** -text
docs/research/human-template-reuse/evidence/host-proof/** -text

# VR-1B WP3-HOST-01 evidence folder (2026-11-27).
#
# Same rationale as the folder above: the folder mixes text (CSV measurement
# tables, markdown reports, run logs) with PNG renders, so `-text` is used to
# switch end-of-line conversion off in both directions. This keeps the measured
# numbers byte-identical for a reviewer who re-runs the same comparison on
# Linux or macOS, and keeps the PNG bytes untouched.
docs/phases/P1-visual-recovery/evidence/vr1b-wp3-host-01/** -text

